<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-16"?>
<Task version="1.4" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <!--
    Samples the demand monitor every 6 hours, whether or not the app is open.

    WHY A SCHEDULED TASK: a 7-day trend is a measurement of the GAPS between
    observations, so the monitor must run unattended. An in-process timer only
    runs while uvicorn is up, and uvicorn is started by hand.

    COST: one eBay Browse call per alert-enabled tracked product per run.
    ~20 products every 6h is ~80 calls/day against a 5,000/day allowance.

    ENCODING: Task Scheduler's XML reader requires genuine UTF-16, and fails
    with "unable to switch the encoding" on a UTF-8 file. Convert before use -
    recipe verified on this machine, PowerShell 5.1, 2026-10-20 (the earlier
    XmlDocument.Save($path, 'UTF-16') form does not bind there: "Cannot find
    an overload for Save and the argument count: 2"):

      $content = Get-Content backend\scripts\schedule_demand_monitor.xml -Raw
      [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText("$env:TEMP\dm_task.xml", $content, [System.Text.Encoding]::Unicode)
      schtasks /create /tn "eBayHunter Demand Monitor" /xml "$env:TEMP\dm_task.xml" /f

    The PowerShell cmdlets (Register-ScheduledTask / Import-ScheduledTask) are
    NOT used: this machine has the ScheduledTasks module's manifest but not its
    native DLL, so every cmdlet in that module is missing. schtasks.exe works.

    XML is used rather than `schtasks /create /tr` because the CLI splits the
    /tr value at the first space when the quoting does not survive the shell:
    the repo lives under "C:\Users\Agha Moutsim\", and a CLI registration that
    looks successful can end up running a file called "C:\Users\Agha" and fail
    every run with 0x80070002. XML carries the path as an element, so it cannot
    be split. (Verified here by hitting exactly that failure first.)

    The task runs as the logged-on user with NO stored password. It therefore
    does not run while you are logged out. Change <LogonType> to PasswordOnly
    and Task Scheduler will ask for your Windows password, which it stores
    encrypted - do not commit that variant.
  -->
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <Description>Samples one real eBay sold-count per tracked product, so the 7-day Hot Items trend is built from real observations instead of staying unverified.</Description>
    <URI>\ebay-hunter\demand-monitor</URI>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <Triggers>
    <CalendarTrigger>
      <StartBoundary>2026-10-03T06:00:00</StartBoundary>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ScheduleByDay>
        <DaysInterval>1</DaysInterval>
      </ScheduleByDay>
      <!-- every 6 hours, repeating daily -->
      <Repetition>
        <Interval>PT6H</Interval>
        <Duration>P1D</Duration>
        <StopAtDurationEnd>false</StopAtDurationEnd>
      </Repetition>
    </CalendarTrigger>
  </Triggers>
  <Principals>
    <Principal id="Author">
      <UserId>S-1-5-21-4027038600-626433640-3063675340-1002</UserId>
      <LogonType>InteractiveToken</LogonType>
      <RunLevel>LeastPrivilege</RunLevel>
    </Principal>
  </Principals>
  <Settings>
    <!-- never stack two runs if one is still going -->
    <MultipleInstancesPolicy>IgnoreNew</MultipleInstancesPolicy>
    <DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>false</DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>
    <StopIfGoingOnBatteries>false</StopIfGoingOnBatteries>
    <!-- if the machine was asleep or logged off at the scheduled time, run as
         soon as it can: the gaps between samples are the measurement, so a
         skipped run is a hole in the data -->
    <StartWhenAvailable>true</StartWhenAvailable>
    <Enabled>true</Enabled>
    <Hidden>false</Hidden>
    <IdleSettings>
      <StopOnIdleEnd>false</StopOnIdleEnd>
      <RestartOnIdle>false</RestartOnIdle>
    </IdleSettings>
    <!-- a stuck run must not block the next one forever -->
    <ExecutionTimeLimit>PT30M</ExecutionTimeLimit>
    <Priority>7</Priority>
  </Settings>
  <Actions Context="Author">
    <Exec>
      <Command>C:\Users\Agha Moutsim\Desktop\ebay-hunter\backend\scripts\run_demand_monitor.cmd</Command>
      <WorkingDirectory>C:\Users\Agha Moutsim\Desktop\ebay-hunter\backend</WorkingDirectory>
    </Exec>
  </Actions>
</Task>